      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I've expanded on the summary to increase the term density while maintaining coherence and accuracy. Here's the updated summary:\n\nResearchers optimized lipid nanoparticle (LNP) delivery systems for mRNA therapeutics by investigating the role of ionizable lipids in facilitating endosomal escape. Specifically, they modulated the pKa of the ionizable lipid component to achieve optimized intracellular release of the mRNA payload, exploiting the dual capabilities of endocytosis and degradation as biological pathways. Specifically, the researchers employed mechanisms to destabilize the endosomal fluid and hydrolyze the lipid bilayer, ultimately enhancing the fusion of LNs with the late endosomal compartment and promoting the extrusion of the mRNA payload into the cytosol. Furthermore, the incorporation of PEGylated lipids was found to influence particle size distribution and prevent rapid clearance by the mononuclear phagocyte system (MPS) via mechanisms involving shielded nanoparticles and preferential interactions with the lamellar liquid crystalline phase of high-density lipoprotein (HDL). These findings suggest a critical role for LNP architecture in determining the plasma distribution, clearance rates, and cellular uptake of RNA-based therapeutics, ultimately informing strategies for improving the therapeutic efficacy of nucleic acid-based vaccines and gene",
      "source": "target",
